; The phonemes for the front end. Finished words (phonemes, -20) with -1 inside spelled ones, pauses (-2 to -5),
; the end (-9) in; out, the words with -1 between them (put off until the next word's first phoneme, and dropped
; when a pause comes first, as text_to_phonemes.py's '#'), the pauses, a period at the end if the text did not end
; a sentence, and -9. lc is the last card sent; st is 1 inside a word.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   x        03-28: a phoneme: a word's first after another word puts -1 before it
  04                    CLA   x
  05                    SUB   c30
  06                    TAC   neg
  07                    CLA   st
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    TAC   fst
  10                    JMP   ph
  11            fst     CLA   00
  12                    STO   st
  13                    CLA   z
  14                    SUB   lc
  15                    TAC   setp
  16                    JMP   ph
  17            setp    CLA   00
  18                    STO   pend
  19            ph      CLA   pend
  20                    SUB   00
  21                    TAC   o
  22                    OUT   m1
  23                    CLA   z
  24                    STO   pend
  25            o       OUT   x
  26                    CLA   x
  27                    STO   lc
  28                    JMP   rec
  29            neg     CLA   x        29-59: a word's end, -1, a pause, or the end
  30                    ADD   n9
  31                    TAC   w20
  32                    SUB   00
  33                    TAC   end
  34                    CLA   x
  35                    ADD   00
  36                    TAC   pun
  37                    OUT   x
  38                    CLA   x
  39                    STO   lc
  40                    JMP   rec
  41            pun     CLA   z
  42                    STO   pend
  43                    OUT   x
  44                    CLA   x
  45                    STO   lc
  46                    JMP   rec
  47            w20     CLA   st
  48                    SUB   00
  49                    TAC   w0
  50                    JMP   wz
  51            w0      CLA   z
  52                    SUB   lc
  53                    TAC   setp2
  54                    JMP   wz
  55            setp2   CLA   00
  56                    STO   pend
  57            wz      CLA   z
  58                    STO   st
  59                    JMP   rec
  60            end     CLA   pend     60-75: the end: a -1 put off, a period if needed, -9
  61                    SUB   00
  62                    TAC   chk
  63                    OUT   m1
  64                    CLA   m1
  65                    STO   lc
  66            chk     CLA   lc
  67                    ADD   n5
  68                    TAC   per
  69                    CLA   lc
  70                    ADD   n3
  71                    SUB   00
  72                    TAC   fin
  73            per     OUT   m3
  74            fin     OUT   m9
  75                    HRS   00
  80            x       DATA  0
  81            st      DATA  0
  82            lc      DATA  0
  83            pend    DATA  0
  84            z       DATA  0
  85            c30     DATA  30
  86            n9      DATA  9
  87            n5      DATA  5
  88            n3      DATA  3
  89            m1      DATA  -1
  90            m3      DATA  -3
  91            m9      DATA  -9
